I also think wands of wishing should go.  Between magic lamps, smoky
potions, and thrones there are plenty of wishes available in the 
dungeon.  At the very least, make them unrechargeable--seven wishes
from a single wand is a huge number.  Change the wand in the castle
to a magic lamp.

Also, the monsters that are challenging in the end game are exactly
the ones that get genocided.  Maybe scrolls of genocide should have
a chance of failing that goes up with the monster level?

Maybe the Wizard of Yendor should have an amulet of reflection so wands
of death don't work?  That would make him more of a threat.

Finally, maybe bags of holding should go!  This would force players to
pay more attention to what they carry.  I'm usually carrying enough
items to stock a mall at the end of the game.  Perhaps some items
would have to be made lighter to keep the game winnable.

All of these I think would make the game more interesting at higher levels
without having much effect on early games (except you couldn't find a wand
of wishing on level 1 anymore).  On the other hand, I'm not sure I would
have ever finished the game if the higher levels were much more difficult.
I could probably handle them now with everything I've learned, but I might
have given up long ago.  Perhaps the game should be made smaller, but
with more variety.  I think lots of people find the many maze levels
boring.  Cut down on the number of levels you have to traverse in a 
single game, but increase the number of special levels that get added
either randomly or based on your character class.

